N2  -  This study investigates the clinical application of bacteriophage therapy in severeinfections through a prospective, randomized, multi‐center trial targetingventilator‐associated pneumonia (VAP) caused by multidrug‐resistant Gram‐negativebacteria. The trial will comprehensively assess the efficacy, safety, and applicabilityof inhaled bacteriophage cocktail therapy, providing high‐quality clinical evidence tosupport the establishment of an evidence‐based framework for phage therapy. The primaryendpoint is clinical response rate, with secondary endpoints including bacterialclearance and 28‐day mortality, aiming to determine the therapeutic potential andclinical value of phage cocktails in VAP treatment.
