N2  -  We designed and synthesized a medium‐firm drug‐candidate library of cryptand‐like structures possessing a randomized peptide linker on the bacteriophage T7. From the macrocyclic library with a 109 diversity, we obtained a binder toward a cancer‐related protein (Hsp90) with an antibody‐like strong affinity (KD = 62 nM) and the binding was driven by the enthalpy. The selected supramolecular ligand inhibited Hsp90 activity by site‐specific binding outside of the well‐known ATP‐binding pocket on the N‐terminal domain (NTD).
